# Dirtree: Stateful directory trees in the CLI for humans and LLMs. https://github.com/pmarreck/dirtree
ver=1.2
annotate=[
	.mechatron-prime/targets = Declares the exact Nix package and full-suite check built by Mechatron Prime CI.
	LEARNINGS.md = Hard-won sqlite-vec UBSan and pure Nix sandbox execution lessons
	MISTAKES.md = Agent workflow mistakes and corrective lessons
	PLAN.md = Current checked CI repair plan with completion times and curiosity pokes
	README.md = Project overview, installation, testing, usage, and configuration documentation
	build.zig = Build: links sqlite3/sqlite_vec0 and wires aggregated plus per-module unit tests
	flake.nix = Nix package, dependency cache, dev shell, and sandboxed full-suite CI derivation
	src/indexer.zig = Incremental conversation indexer with batched embedding generation, resumable missing-vector repair, and progress reporting.
	src/ollama.zig = Ollama HTTP adapter; verifies installed models and actively warms idle models with a readiness embedding.
	src/storage.zig = SQLite/sqlite-vec persistence, including bounded retrieval of messages missing semantic embeddings.
	test = Full runner: build, ReleaseSafe Zig tests, CLI integration, and non-recursive Nix-check mode
	tests/ci_contract = CI-honesty control for build, ReleaseSafe tests, CLI tests, portable CPU, and failure propagation
	tests/cli/fixtures/conversations = Committed conversation fixture (alpha/beta/gamma projects) used to build a deterministic index for CLI tests
	tests/cli/package_artifact_test.sh = Smoke-tests that the exact package artifact copied by ./build executes on the host.
	tests/cli/search_cli_test.sh = CLI integration tests: default scoping, --all, --project partial path/name, env overrides, verbose messaging over a fixture index
]
